      "content": "The platitudes of \"it gets better\" are so hollow because they don't acknowledge the permanent shift you've experienced. What you're describing isn't just a slump; it's the aftermath of a fundamental change, and that loss is real. Instead of waiting for something to happen, maybe you could focus on the quiet, the stillness, and just let yourself be where you are right now. There is a profound, quiet kind of dignity in simply existing when everything else feels like it has ended.",
